1. Git Cherrypick:
    Git cherrypick is basically used to apply the specific commit changes to another branch.

    For Example:
    You are in feature branch and edit one file and push that to feature branch.
    Get the commit id using the git ---> git log --oneline
    After that checkout to main or any branch where we need to apply this specific commit and run below command.
    git cherry-pick <copied commit id from feature branch>
    git push --all (to push the chnages to remote repo)

    